 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "Farewell, my dear boy! When haply away\nThe day has flown and I sleep no tomorrow,\nMy eyes are dim as a rosy ray\nThat gilds my cheeks; the drowsy light below\nBegins to lighten each spirit away;\nYet, perchance, yet, some one may chance agree\nTo bring me back again by an essay\nOf those lost chains which now bind me wholly;\nAnd if you can afford it, \"last away,\nAnd be with us--with us till salvation\nIs passed from earth into heaven,\" may,\nGod grant your prayer, that we may meet again.",
